      en: "Mnarani Ruins is a notable historical in Kenya and ranks among the country's most geographically and culturally significant locations. The ruins of an ancient Arab settlement with two historic mosques and several complex pillar tombs located on Kilifi Creek. Its position close to long-established trade and migration routes has shaped its role in East African history and economy for many generations. Today the natural variety of the surrounding region is closely intertwined with local settlements, agriculture, and scientific research. For learners exploring the Plizio world, Mnarani Ruins offers a clear example of how geography, climate, and culture interact in Kenya and influence the daily lives of its people. Geography and natural science K7–K8 — East African spaces and their functions."
